ShaguPlates libcast -- cast detection
MIT License
Copyright (c) 2016-2021 Eric Mauser (Shagu)

Used by: modules/casts.lua

1.12 has no UnitCastingInfo and no UnitChannelInfo -- they arrive in 2.0 -- so
every vanilla addon drawing a cast bar for anything but the player has built this
layer itself. libcast is the one followed here: the event set, the split between
the player's exact casts and everybody else's parsed ones, and the decision to
key the store by unit **name** rather than by token.

That last one is the load-bearing choice and it is Shagu's. A nameplate has a
name and no unit token, so a library keyed by token would have been target-only
and cast bars would work on one plate out of forty.

**One deliberate departure: the spell database is not ported.** ShaguPlates ships
every spell in the game with its cast time, per locale, which is thousands of
lines to carry and keep current. This learns instead -- every spell the player
casts reports its exact duration to the client, and mobs cast a great many of the
same spells that players do. A spell not yet known draws a full bar with its name
on it, which is the useful half of a cast bar, and fills properly from the first
time the player casts it.

The learned times are account-wide beside the roster and the vendor prices, on
the same argument: a cast time is a fact about the world rather than a setting.
Longest-seen wins, because a cast shortens with haste and lengthens with nothing.

