TurtleMail -- the mailbox
by shirsig / sica, version 1.4.5

Used by: Mail/ -- TurtleMail.lua, TurtleMail.xml, Calendar.lua, the five
localisation files and the three textures

**The bundled tree carries no LICENSE file** and no copyright line in any source
file, the TOC or the README. Open source confirmed by the maintainer of this
addon; recorded here rather than assumed, for the same reason as QuestHaste and
DragonflightUI above -- the absence is real and the next person to read this
deserves to know it was checked rather than skipped.

Unlike those two, this one is **carried whole rather than ported**: it is a
finished mailbox, it works, and there was nothing to gain by rewriting it into
this addon's shapes. What is here is upstream 1.4.5 with the fixes below, each
of which is commented at the point it was made.

  * **`ADDON_LOADED` rejected the only event it would ever get.** The guard
    compared `arg1` against "TurtleMail", and inside this addon the name the
    client announces is "EquadisClassicOverhaul" -- so everything below that
    line, the saved-variable merge included, simply never ran. Both names are
    accepted, so a copy of the file dropped back into a standalone folder still
    works.

  * **The first-open setup was a one-shot that could fail once and never run
    again.** The flag was set before the work, and the work reaches into
    `SendMailPackageButton`'s regions by position; missing regions raised, which
    aborted the whole of `MAIL_SHOW`. The flag now records whether the setup
    succeeded.

  * **The autocomplete list was aged against the wrong clock.** Names are
    stamped and dropped after thirty days, and both halves used `GetTime` --
    seconds since the client started, not a date. Nothing was ever pruned, by
    anybody, ever. `time()` now, with the old session-number stamps re-stamped
    rather than deleted.

  * **A failed attachment left the send half-run.** The item was taken off the
    front of the list and the early return put it back nowhere and left
    `sendmail_sending` set, so the item vanished from the letter and the run
    never ended. Reported as mail not sending until a reload.

  * **`string.match` is Lua 5.1 and 1.12 is 5.0.** One call site, replaced with
    `gsub`.

  * **Two copies stop the game loading.** Both share the global `TurtleMail`
    table and each build registers the same events, so `PLAYER_LOGIN` runs twice
    and the hook installer -- which is not idempotent -- records its own hook as
    the original and calls itself. Unbounded recursion during load-in. It cannot
    be guarded from the inside, because "EquadisClassicOverhaul" sorts first and
    the standalone copy overwrites the guard; so the bundled copy asks
    `GetAddOnInfo` whether the standalone is enabled and stands down if it is.

**Added rather than fixed**: names can be pinned to the top of the autocomplete
list or forgotten from it, with the two gestures and the pin state said on the
row's own tooltip.
